(# Backend Concepts Guide \(Project Walkthrough\)) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(## 1\) What is Backend Development?) Tj
T*
(Backend handles:) Tj
T*
(- Business logic \(rules\)) Tj
T*
(- Data storage/retrieval) Tj
T*
(- Authentication/authorization) Tj
T*
(- API contracts for frontend/mobile clients) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(You can think of backend as "the brain + memory" of an application.) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(## 2\) Project Architecture Used Here) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(We use a layered pattern:) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(1. **Routes**: URL + HTTP method mapping) Tj
T*
(2. **Controllers**: HTTP-level handling \(`req`, `res`\)) Tj
T*
(3. **Services**: Business rules and workflows) Tj
T*
(4. **Repositories**: Data access and persistence details) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(Why this matters:) Tj
T*
(- Easier to read and maintain) Tj
T*
(- Easier to test) Tj
T*
(- Easier to swap tools \(e.g. file DB -> PostgreSQL\)) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(Alternative options:) Tj
T*
(- MVC-only style \(simpler, but can become messy as project grows\)) Tj
T*
(- Clean Architecture / Hexagonal \(more scalable but more complex\)) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(## 3\) Authentication \(Signed Token\)) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(Flow:) Tj
T*
(1. User logs in with email/password.) Tj
T*
(2. Backend verifies credentials.) Tj
T*
(3. Backend returns signed token.) Tj
T*
(4. Client sends token in `Authorization` header.) Tj
T*
(5. Backend verifies token before protected routes.) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(Why signed token?) Tj
T*
(- Stateless) Tj
T*
(- Common pattern across frontend/mobile/microservices) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(Other options:) Tj
T*
(- Server sessions + cookies) Tj
T*
(- OAuth \(Google/GitHub login\)) Tj
T*
( ) Tj
T*
(When to use:) Tj
T*
(- Token-based auth is great for API-based apps.) Tj
T*
(- Session cookies are good for traditional server-rendered apps.) Tj
T*
ET
